    {
      "name": "🔌 Socket.io Events (reference)",
      "description": "The client connects via `useAuthStore.connectSocket()` → `io(BASE_URL, { query: { userId } })` with `BASE_URL = http://localhost:5001` in development. These are **not REST requests** — they document the real-time contract for testing with a Socket.io client (e.g. Postman's WebSocket request).\n\n| Event | Direction | Payload | Handled in |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `connection` | Client → Server | query `userId` | `useAuthStore.connectSocket` |\n| `getOnlineUsers` | Server → Client | `string[]` userIds | `useAuthStore` → `onlineUsers` |\n| `newMessage` | Server → Client | `Message` | `useChatStore.subscribeToMessages` |\n| `messageDelivered` | Client → Server | `{ messageId, senderId }` | `useChatStore.subscribeToMessages` |\n| `messageRead` | Client → Server | `{ messageId, senderId }` | ChatContainer (on open) |\n| `markAllMessagesAsRead` | Client → Server | `{ senderId, receiverId }` | `useChatStore.markMessagesAsRead` |\n| `messageStatusUpdate` | Server → Client | `{ messageId, status }` | `useChatStore.updateMessageStatus` |\n| `allMessagesRead` | Server → Client | `{ receiverId }` | Chat header ticks |\n\nTo test: open a **WebSocket request** in Postman to `ws://localhost:5001/socket.io/?EIO=4&transport=websocket` and complete the Socket.io handshake, or use two browser tabs of the running app.",
      "item": []
    }
